1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:04,154
This is the Robo Cranes, from Grulla Elementary!

2
00:00:04,554 --> 00:00:09,434
Last season, we made it all the way to the VEX World Championship.

3
00:00:09,834 --> 00:00:12,452
This year, the game is Level Up.

4
00:00:12,852 --> 00:00:18,132
We stack bean bags higher and higher, and we learn something new every day.

5
00:00:18,532 --> 00:00:19,538
Let's go!

6
00:00:24,233 --> 00:00:29,153
Hi Robo Cranes! I'm Cranebot, and this is Flop, our robot!

7
00:00:29,553 --> 00:00:32,648
Flop has five parts, just like a body.

8
00:00:33,148 --> 00:00:36,951
Wheels are Flop's legs: they drive and turn.

9
00:00:37,451 --> 00:00:42,748
The intake is Flop's mouth: it grabs bean bags and spits them out.

10
00:00:43,248 --> 00:00:50,018
The arm is Flop's neck: it lifts bags up high, just like my long crane neck!

11
00:00:50,518 --> 00:00:55,368
The camera is Flop's eyes: it sees red, blue and yellow.

12
00:00:55,868 --> 00:00:58,679
And the bumper is Flop's nose: boop!

13
00:00:59,379 --> 00:01:03,876
Five parts, one robot, one team. Let's build it!

14
00:01:12,867 --> 00:01:16,454
How do we score in Level Up? With bean bags!

15
00:01:17,154 --> 00:01:20,390
Drop a bean bag in the floor goal: one point.

16
00:01:20,990 --> 00:01:24,077
Put it on top of the pyramid: three points!

17
00:01:24,677 --> 00:01:26,234
Now here's the secret.

18
00:01:26,634 --> 00:01:33,296
Put a bag ON TOP of another bag on the pyramid, and it reaches the next level: six points!

19
00:01:33,646 --> 00:01:34,738
That's double!

20
00:01:35,438 --> 00:01:41,198
So the best teams drop every bag in the exact same spot, so they stack.

21
00:01:41,698 --> 00:01:45,985
One, three, six. Higher means more points!

22
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:58,331
Bean bags come in three colors.

23
00:01:58,731 --> 00:02:00,841
Red bags go on the red goal.

24
00:02:03,241 --> 00:02:05,533
Blue bags go on the blue goal.

25
00:02:06,133 --> 00:02:08,944
And yellow? Yellow is WILD!

26
00:02:09,294 --> 00:02:11,116
It counts on any goal.

27
00:02:11,516 --> 00:02:16,633
If a bag is the wrong color, or still touching the robot, it's zero points.

28
00:02:17,233 --> 00:02:20,375
Match the color, let it go, and score!

29
00:02:29,367 --> 00:02:35,290
Flop can do things one at a time: drive... stop... then lift the arm.

30
00:02:35,690 --> 00:02:37,022
That's slow!

31
00:02:37,522 --> 00:02:42,841
Or Flop can do two things at once: lift the arm WHILE it drives.

32
00:02:43,341 --> 00:02:48,748
In VEXcode, click the little arrow on the arm block and pick 'and don't wait.'

33
00:02:49,148 --> 00:02:51,655
Now the next block starts right away.

34
00:02:52,155 --> 00:02:55,515
It's like walking and chewing gum at the same time.

35
00:02:56,015 --> 00:03:00,771
Save a second here, a second there, and you'll have time for more bean bags!

36
00:03:09,967 --> 00:03:13,682
Every time Flop turns, it can be a tiny bit wrong.

37
00:03:14,082 --> 00:03:16,482
One little mistake is okay.

38
00:03:16,982 --> 00:03:21,682
But after many turns, the mistakes add up, and Flop gets lost!

39
00:03:22,082 --> 00:03:27,602
The fix: instead of 'turn right 90,' use 'turn to heading.'

40
00:03:28,002 --> 00:03:32,018
That means 'face that direction,' like 'face the window.'

41
00:03:32,418 --> 00:03:37,058
Flop checks its compass every time, so mistakes don't pile up.

42
00:03:37,458 --> 00:03:38,818
Smart robot!

43
00:03:45,534 --> 00:03:47,658
This year, it's your turn.

44
00:03:48,008 --> 00:03:53,848
We'll build a robot, code a robot, drive a robot, and do it as a team.

45
00:03:54,198 --> 00:03:55,398
Are you ready?

46
00:03:56,098 --> 00:03:58,418
Robo Cranes, let's go!

